      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Consider the system of linear equations \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-6x+8y=-46 \\\\ 6x+5y=20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $y$ can be written as \n$y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{|\\begin{aligned}-6 & 8 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{aligned}|},$ \nwhere ${D}_{y}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-6x+8y=-46 \\\\ 6x+5y=20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}-6 & \\,8 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}-6 & -46 \\\\ 6 & 20\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$",
